WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.700
Here are the photos of the damage to your shingles.

00:02.700 --> 00:06.000
Anything I have circled means it's hail damage.

00:06.000 --> 00:07.900
This is exactly what we look for

00:07.900 --> 00:09.840
when we're looking for hail damage.

00:09.840 --> 00:12.740
If you notice the divot is circular in nature,

00:12.740 --> 00:15.620
even if this damage doesn't look like a big deal,

00:15.620 --> 00:17.140
what happens over time,

00:17.140 --> 00:20.340
these hail divots fill with water, freeze.

00:20.340 --> 00:23.660
When water freezes, it expands and breaks apart the shingle,

00:23.660 --> 00:25.760
which will eventually lead to leaks.

00:25.760 --> 00:28.400
That is why your insurance company is responsible

00:28.400 --> 00:30.920
and your policy covers this type of damage.

